    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Captain John Coffeen became the first permanent settler of Cavendish when he brought his family into the wilderness in June 1769.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cavendish%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Salmon Dutton and Leonard Proctor founded the two major settlements of Cavendish and Proctorsville in the early 1780s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cavendishvt.com/cavendish-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the early 1800s, Cavendish hosted a variety of businesses, including three gristmills, eight saw mills, and two woolen factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cavendishvt.com/cavendish-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The arrival of railroads ended sheep farming in Cavendish by allowing cheaper wool to be imported from larger ranches in the West.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cavendishvt.com/cavendish-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Author and dissident Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn lived in Cavendish from 1977 to 1994.",
